  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "SDK Version: 3.1.10\n\nDescription of the bug: The amount of text allowed for an Avatar Parameter seems to be determined by the size of the window pane of the parameter list. If the text exceeds a certain amount of the displayed box width, it will get truncated from the front. Expanding the size of the parameter window pane so that the text fits within the field seems to resolve this.\n\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n\n1. Create a parameter with a long name while your parameter list window is at the default width or shorter. The parameter name length must exceed the displayed width.\n\n2. If the parameter name is long enough, you will see it truncate from the front end of the label.\n\n3. Expand the width of the parameter pane and re-attempt adding the long name.\n\nAlternatively....\n\n1. Expand the parameter pane and create a parameter with a really long name.\n\n2. Click into another field so that it commits.\n\n3. Shrink the parameter pane.\n\n4. Click the label of your long parameter and observe the truncation.\n\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots): N/A",
